## sconce

<https://github.com/whit3rabbit/mlx-v>, commit `0abccca`, `Cargo.toml`
declaring `license = "MIT"` (the repository ships no `LICENSE` file, so
there is no license text to quote here as the entry above does).

| here | upstream | what changed |
|---|---|---|
| `crates/vision-io/src/rounding.rs` | `src/vision/rounding.rs` | taken whole; the doc comment re-derived for this family's factor of 32 |
| `crates/vision-io/src/resize.rs` | `src/vision/preprocess.rs` | the PIL arm only. The torchvision arm and its per-axis precision search are dropped (no checkpoint here resizes with it), as is the unclamped f64 value path (this port's position embedding interpolates from an index/weight table rather than resampling). Rewritten against interleaved RGB8 slices, so candle's `Tensor` is gone with it |
| `crates/vision-io/src/smart_resize.rs` | `src/vision/preprocess.rs` | `resized_dims`, minus the explicit-override variant. sconce's trailing `.max(factor)` on both axes is dropped in favour of refusing a zero edge by name |
| `crates/vision-io/src/patchify.rs` | `src/vision/patchify.rs` | the merge-window nest, with the INNER feature order changed from `(C, T, P, P)` to `(T, P, P, C)`. Not a port difference to reconcile later: it is what lets the repack copy `patch_embed.proj.weight` verbatim (`docs/VISION_PHASE0.md` item 4), and `crates/vision-io/tests/preprocess_parity.rs` bridges it explicitly |

**`src/models/qwen2_vl/mrope.rs` was read and deliberately not taken.** It
drives its walk from `vision_start` markers where mlx-vlm's `get_rope_index`
drives from the image-pad token's own position. The two agree on every
well-formed prompt and disagree on a malformed one, and this port follows
mlx-vlm because mlx-vlm is the reference for the trunk being fed. The
divergence is pinned by
`a_placeholder_with_no_vision_start_is_treated_as_text`.

## Bundled fonts

Three font families ship inside the macOS app's resource bundle, under
`swift/TurboSparkApp/Sources/TurboSparkApp/Resources/Fonts/`. All three are
licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, whose terms permit
bundling them in a larger work; each family's full license text sits beside
the faces it covers, which is what the OFL requires.

Unlike every other entry on this page, no code was adapted from these
projects. They are unmodified binary assets, carried so that the Appearance
pane's font pickers cannot offer a family that then fails to render: macOS
does not ship any of the three, and `Font.custom` falls back to the system
face silently rather than erroring. `swift/CLAUDE.md` Gotcha 22 is the same
rule on the model hub's filters: build the options from what is present.

Four faces of each (Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold), 3.8 MB in total.

| family | upstream | version | license file here |
|---|---|---|---|
| Inter | <https://github.com/rsms/inter> | v4.1 | `OFL-Inter.txt` |
| JetBrains Mono | <https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono> | v2.304 | `OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt` |
| Fira Code | <https://github.com/tonsky/FiraCode> | v6.2 | `OFL-FiraCode.txt` |

